{"title":"Career Roadmap · Diagnostics Executive","role":"Diagnostics Executive","summary":"A Diagnostics Executive works within the diagnostic healthcare ecosystem, supporting the delivery, coordination, promotion, implementation or operation of diagnostic services.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Genetic Counselling / Medical Biotechnology"},"about":[{"label":"Important","text":"“Diagnostics Executive” is a broad industry-facing role. Depending on the employer, it can involve diagnostic-laboratory operations, molecular/genetic testing coordination, diagnostic product support, client coordination, or healthcare business operations. For roles involving direct genetic counselling, molecular testing, or laboratory sign-off, additional specialized qualifications and applicable professional requirements may apply."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Diagnostics Executive works within the diagnostic healthcare ecosystem, supporting the delivery, coordination, promotion, implementation or operation of diagnostic services."},{"type":"p","text":"In a Genetic Counselling / Medical Biotechnology pathway, the professional can develop expertise in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Molecular diagnostics"},{"text":"Genetic testing"},{"text":"Laboratory workflows"},{"text":"Diagnostic test interpretation"},{"text":"Patient/sample coordination"},{"text":"Clinical laboratory communication"},{"text":"Diagnostic product support"},{"text":"Healthcare operations"},{"text":"Genetic and genomic technologies"},{"text":"Data and reporting"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on the organisation, the role may sit between clinical teams, laboratories, diagnostic companies, hospitals and patients/clients."},{"type":"h","text":"Career Flow"},{"type":"h","text":"Medical Biotechnology / Genetics Foundation"},{"type":"h","text":"Laboratory + Diagnostic Trainin